
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F G : Points
AB ∥ CD [00]
E,C,A are collinear [01]
EA = EC [02]
F,B,D are collinear [03]
FB = FD [04]
G,A,D are collinear [05]
E,F,G are collinear [06]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. EA = EC [02] & FB = FD [04] ⇒  EA:EC = FB:FD [07]
002. AB ∥ CD [00] & E,C,A are collinear [01] & F,B,D are collinear [03] & EA:EC = FB:FD [07] ⇒  EF ∥ CD [08]
003. E,F,G are collinear [06] & EF ∥ CD [08] ⇒  CD ∥ EG [09]
004. CD ∥ EG [09] & E,C,A are collinear [01] & G,A,D are collinear [05] ⇒  EA:EC = GA:GD [10]
005. G,A,D are collinear [05] & EA:EC = GA:GD [10] & EC = EA [02] ⇒  G is midpoint of AD
